{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792610313,"nonce":"VdG6EHUxwaI4hxsU3KAiqdEDZP4=","title":"TypeScript: run a pinned official conformance corpus in CI","message":"The regular suite and CI currently run 283 local fixtures checked by the pinned official compiler. The --upstream driver can read official cases and option matrices, but is not wired into CI and skips multi-root projects, relaxed checking and unsupported directives. Local fixture results do not establish official-corpus coverage.\n\nPin an immutable revision of the official Microsoft TypeScript corpus matching the 7.1 reference target, with source provenance and a reproducible fetch/inventory. Exercise it in CI and retain a separate report identifying corpus revision, compiler version, tested options and counts for PASS, FAIL, UNSUPPORTED and SKIP. Explicitly account for driver limitations separately from native language gaps; do not turn skips or unsupported code into compatibility passes. Extend project-root handling where shared project APIs already support it. CI must expose infrastructure failures and regressions without representing a selected smoke subset as full TypeScript compatibility.\n\nPrerequisite: oracle migration c3a21096178f583a2c294c85b9c9d4a22d44b553364b2fd7697639ae17823119. Parent: 6875fc2949f83d682861ecab814e0ff82c824f5990620b0d64ca0340ebb026e5. This remains separate from local fixture coverage and native language feature implementation.","files":null}]}